            <ArticleTitle>[Pseudocoronary syndrome in reflux esophagitis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>11-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors have shown that among 173 patients with the insufficient closing function of the cardia there were 18 patients with pseudo-coronary syndrome related with reflux-esophagitis. Operations were performed on 14 of them with good effects. The surgical correction of insufficiency of cardia functions in most cases gives elimination of cardio-vascular disorders resulting from reflux-esophagitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
